 "structural_change": "dsdv_eng_rr_b3m (STW-S81c-COLLA3 10-22, MAIN; from dsdv_eng_rr_b2 @c9c114fd3, same RTL @b8508b4d3 / pins / macros / 561.6 outline / cycles): one TritonCTS tree over 59,180 sinks -> k-means regional CTS (clock_split_km, K=32, port ck). Why: the b2 --cts gate (gold2 20261022-065614) FAILED only clock_rule: TT insertion 666.8..886.7 ps, pin-flop spread TT 121.4 / FF 116.4 ps (trial GRT overflow 0, native32 PASS, setup at placement -28 ps reg->reg = repairable). Same class + fix as dscoll_lane s8nk -> s8nq/s8nr (K=16 83-88 ps -> K=24/32 55/52) and xrt3t: equal-load local roots under the balanced top tree. No constraint relaxed. | b2 FB (STW-S81c-COLLA 10-22): dsdv_eng_rr_b @b8508b4d3 (census-fixed source, gate passed native+CTS: TT spread 59.8/FF 55.5) FAILED trial GRT: GRT-0183 maze router boxed in during the post-repair incremental route (initial overflow 0, M3 22.8%, fill 46% at 518.4). Same RTL/pins/macro positions, outline 518.4 -> 561.6 (fill ~39%) for local routing room. Prev: S81-ELEM2-ENGRR 10-21 successor of Codex R6 80b6d5334 (native PASS32 52120018d; zero-wire intrinsic 082fa3d2b TT -84.4 ps): head rco 3 registered stages (+2 edges request chain, priced) with carry-select adds; XQ wait-line decode registered + line read 1 edge earlier (same AQ age); token map cid range fault 1 edge later; hash_n32 generator all adders 8-bit carry-select. Flat whole-RR cluster: the RA640 lookup has no CLOSED leaf view, so it is placed flat (single ck root, lookup clock pins are ck branches).",
